  "description": "Variation of condition 1 of planning permission dated 07 March 2025 (RN: 24/02294/FULL) for the: Part demolition, part retention (of existing basement and structural frame) and redevelopment to create a building of basement, ground and seven upper floors with rooftop plant and two storey building and single storey infill to courtyard, to provide new hotel with ancillary uses, including restaurant, bar, gym and spa facilities; cycle parking, landscaping and associated works. (Site of former Belgravia Police Station). NAMELY, to allow  increase the number of guestrooms from 205 to 255 (uplift in 50 rooms) through additional partitions; enhance the Front of House (FOH) offering, including an expanded gym, spa and wellness facility in the basement and a farm shop / deli in place of the previously approved bar and restaurant; alterations to rooflights and lightwells to suit the revised room layouts; introduction of a new fire escape from the basement escape stair directly onto Semley Place; changes to door location on Buckingham Palace Road."
